  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "forge_query",
      "description": "Read the brand's Forge: render templates and their git-like revision tree, render sets (rows of values one template renders) and renders. action='templates' lists templates (key, bindingId, name, sourceAssetId). 'template' (templateKey, bindingId when a key is in two workspaces) returns its contract: every variable (key, label, kind, required, options, character budget), the outputs and the contractHash. 'template_tree' (assetId: a template's sourceAssetId) lists its variants — branches, the Original first — with their revisions (commits: parentRevisionId, publications), draft/published heads and the default variant; 'template_revision' (revisionId) returns one with its edits; 'template_layers' (revisionId) lists its comps, layers and what each can edit; 'template_diff' (revisionId → toRevisionId) compares two revisions' edits; 'template_run' (assetId: a revision's sourceAssetId) reads its Forge publishing run (state, needs). 'sources' (limit) lists the brand's uploaded projects, newest first: assetId, name, parseState, forgeState, and templateKey once published — a parsed After Effects source builds on its own (forgeState; publish with forge_manage template_forge) — step='start' only when it has no run; native families (hyperframes, web_component, blender) never enter template_forge. 'sets' (templateKey optional); 'set' (setId) returns rows AND `resolved`, each row's values after inheritance from its parent row, and `settings` — the set's delivery defaults (metaTarget default ad set, Slack and approval rooms, final); 'set_revisions' (setId) lists kept states; 'set_diff' (setId with rowIds=[a,b], or fromRevision and optional toRevision) shows what renders differently. 'destinations' lists Slack rooms and Meta ad accounts (campaigns and ad sets: paid_manage action='hierarchy'). 'jobs' (templateKey/setId/batchId/status/limit) lists renders; 'job' (jobId) refreshes one; 'batch' (render_confirm's batchId, waitSeconds ≤55) answers as soon as every render settles — renders take minutes, so loop it with waitSeconds=50 in a background subagent until done. 'scenes' lists the 3D product scenes. Writes are forge_manage.",
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Read video templates and render sets",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false
      },
