    {
      "name": "forge_manage",
      "description": "Change the brand’s Forge render sets and render them. A render set is rows of variable values for ONE template; a row with parentId inherits its parent’s values and overrides some (a variation). Read first with forge_query. action='set_create' (templateKey, bindingId when the key is in two workspaces, name, rows[{label, overrides, parentId}], description) — row ids are minted when omitted. 'set_update' (setId, expectedRevision from forge_query set, and any of name/description/rows/settings — rows REPLACES the whole list). settings (set_create/set_update; only the keys named change, null clears) are the set's delivery defaults: metaTarget {adAccountId, campaignId, adsetId} — a new PAUSED ad in that ad set for every row without its own target (ids from forge_query destinations and paid_manage action=hierarchy; replacing an existing ad stays a per-row delivery), slackDestinationId, approvalDestinationIds, final. 'set_fork' (setId, name optional) copies a set into a new one. 'set_delete' (setId). 'suggest_rows' drafts rows with AI (brief or documentIds/mediaAssetIds; setId or templateKey; count ceiling and autoCount; varyKeys; parentRowId) and saves NOTHING. Use brand_knowledge action=add_file for small documents, library_manage action=upload_inline for small images, or source_begin for a signed-in upload handoff (documents, images, videos, and template projects: an After Effects package or ZIP, PSD, AI, PowerPoint, HTML, .blend); source_status returns documentIds, mediaAssetIds and templateAssetIds when ready. 'source_figma' (figmaUrl: a Figma frame link imports that frame; a file link lists its frames, then figmaNodeIds up to 5) makes each frame a design template with the brand's Figma connection: a web component that renders as its templateKey (web:<assetId>) with no build. 'apply_suggestions' (setId, expectedRevision, selected rows with their draft ids) appends selected rows once, preserving the rest of the set. 'render_preview' (setId, rowIds optional) checks every row as the Render tab does and returns readiness, destinations (where each row goes: library, new_ad, replace) and a single-use confirmationToken. Omitted slackDestinationId/approvalDestinationIds/final take the set's settings (slackDestinationId null = no post); a row's own delivery wins over the set's metaTarget; anything bound for Meta parks for approval; final=true is a non-proof render, owner/admin only. A refusal a person may override names its flag (acceptMissingFonts, acceptLinkedLineMismatch, acceptOffPaletteColor) in details.overrides — ask the person before passing it. 'render_confirm' (confirmationToken) queues the renders and returns a batchId; wait with forge_query action='batch' from a background subagent. Refusals keep the service's reason (e.g. render_set_revision_conflict: re-read the set). 'rows_patch' (setId, expectedRevision, rows upserted by id — no id appends — and removeRowIds). 'set_create' and 'set_retarget' (setId, expectedRevision) take templateRevisionId, a PUBLISHED revision; 'set_fork' takes revision, a kept state. Templates (forge_query template_tree, template_layers first): 'template_preview' (assetId, parentRevisionId, edits{layers[{compId, layerId, text|font|fontSize|visible|x|y|width|height|rotation|scale|opacity}], slots[{slotKey, defaultValue|publicName|required|exposed|charBudget}], orders[{compId, layerIds}], recolor{palette}}) saves nothing; 'template_save' (the same plus name, a new variant, OR variantId whose head is parentRevisionId) commits; the Original is never rewritten. Owner/admin: 'template_forge' (assetId: the revision's sourceAssetId; step start with templateName, decisions, draft, smoke, promote, resume) publishes it — after start the autopilot smokes and publishes on its own when nothing needs a person, so step in only where template_run parks; a CONFLICT means the run already moved; smoke renders cost money; 'template_set_default' (assetId, variantId). 3D product scenes (forge_query action='scenes'): 'scene_fill' (assetId, versionId, brief{productImageAssetId, headline, price, cta, text}, outputs optional) fills the scene from the brand — logo, palette, a product picture — and the brief, renders NOTHING, and returns the values plus a single-use confirmationToken; 'scene_render' (confirmationToken) queues one render per output into the Library. Poll with the template's scene render history in the Forge.",
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Upload, edit, publish and render video templates",
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "destructiveHint": true,
        "idempotentHint": false,
        "openWorldHint": true
      },
